    {
      "id": 13,
      "act": "unmasking",
      "label": "So who did it?",
      "mood": "reveal",
      "narration": "[serious] For two years, nobody knew who did it. Then, on September 6, 2018, the US Justice Department named a suspect. It charged a North Korean programmer named Park Jin Hyok. Prosecutors say he worked for a hacking team backed by North Korea's government. Experts call that group Lazarus. Prosecutors also link it to the Sony Pictures hack in 2014. He has never been arrested. He's on the FBI's wanted list. The charges have never been tested in court.",
      "visuals": [
